# What NOT to ship to the builder as build context.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. There was no .dockerignore, so every build sent the
# whole repository root. That is 33GB, and almost none of it is a
# build input:
#
#   dist/vm        28G   qemu VM images
#   dist/wheels   5.1G   fetched wheels and generated pip indexes
#   dist/*         ~1G   docs venv, gh-pages worktree, extracted images
#   .git/         444M
#
# On a local builder the transfer is free and the omission was
# invisible for months. On a remote one it is the entire build:
#
#   cupy-wheel on snoc-gaming, gfx950 run 20261127T155149Z
#     [internal] load build context   2467s
#     the RUN step that builds it      156s
#     sccache                          100% hit, 0 misses
#
#   45m47s wall, of which 41 minutes was context transfer and not one
#   line was compiled. gfx1201 reproduced it at 2425s against a 160s
#   RUN step -- the cost is a fixed transfer, so it does not vary with
#   the architecture or the work.
#
# Measured after this file: the context BuildKit sends goes from
# 33GB to 4.4MB, checked by building a throwaway
# `FROM busybox / COPY . /ctx / RUN du -sh /ctx`.
#
# WHAT THE BUILD ACTUALLY NEEDS from the context is docker/ and
# nothing else: every COPY and every --mount=type=bind,source= in
# docker/Dockerfile.* names a path under it (max-jobs.sh,
# auditwheel-rocm.sh, wheel-verdict.py, rocm-prune.sh,
# atom-topk-fallback.py, emu-profile-pack.py, mori-entrypoint.sh,
# packs/, vllm-emu-shim/). The `dist/` strings in those Dockerfiles
# are /opt/pytorch/dist/ inside the image, not host paths.
#
# This file is a deny-list rather than an allow-list on purpose: a
# `*` + `!docker/` pair would silently drop a new context path the day
# someone adds one, and the failure would look like a missing file
# inside a RUN step rather than a dockerignore problem.

# 33GB: VM images, fetched wheels, generated indexes, the gh-pages
# worktree, extracted images. Nothing in a build reads any of it.
dist/

# Not a build input, and the largest thing after dist/.
.git/
.gitignore

# Agent worktrees: whole second checkouts of this repo, one per
# branch, each as large as the repo itself.
.claude/

# Scraped metrics and run artefacts.
telemetry/out/
*.prom

# Local build logs, caches and editor droppings.
*.log
**/__pycache__/
.cache/
.docker/
.builders/generated/
*.swp
*~
